; Tutorial_7_Gather_Files_from_a_Page.inix -- every document on a page, at once.

[about]
Title=7 - Gather Files from a Page
Intro=Alt plus Shift plus W, Web Download, lists the documents on a page by kind, fetches the ones you choose with the browser's own sign-in, and names each as it arrives.
Setup=HomerView is open on a page with documents on it, such as an agency's publications.
Homework=Gather every PDF from a publications page, then open its folder.

[step]

Say=One want: every report on a publications page, without clicking each one.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus Shift plus H opens the HomerView browser, or brings it back.
Key=Alt+Control+Shift+H
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus W, W for Web, is Web Download. HomerView says what is there, by kind.
Key=Alt+Shift+W
Hear=pdf: PDF document, 11. docx: Word document, 6. html: Web page, 1.

[step]

Say=The sensible kinds are already filled in; page addresses are listed but not chosen, since they are many and rarely wanted. Enter fetches.
Key=Enter
Hear=(each file's name as it arrives)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Silence after a name means it arrived; only a failure says more. The request carries the browser's own sign-in, so a file behind a sign-in comes as it would to a click.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=At the end, a message box gives the count, the folder, and anything that did not come.
Key=
Hear=(the count of files, and their folder)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=They go to the page's own folder under Downloads, and names are unescaped first, so Annual percent 20 Report arrives as Annual Report. A planned misstep: running it again adds to the folder rather than replacing it.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Every document on a page.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus W
